00:29:39,680 --> 00:29:41,940
Oh, Lord, they're turning into flames.

563
00:29:42,040 --> 00:29:43,340
Well, I thought it was magnificent.

564
00:29:43,440 --> 00:29:46,600
I heard it, but, and knew it was a broken

565
00:29:46,620 --> 00:29:50,520
I couldn't quite understand this national hysteria

566
00:29:50,620 --> 00:29:54,920
and people rushing out to dig a hole, you know, to get in.

567
00:29:55,020 --> 00:29:57,060
Orson Welles had just directed the famous

568
00:29:57,160 --> 00:29:59,160
War of the Worlds radio broadcast,

569
00:29:59,260 --> 00:30:01,860
the dramatic show that frightened millions of Americans

570
00:30:01,960 --> 00:30:04,980
into believing the country actually was being invaded

